<Base title="Terms of use">
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 8 September 2026</p>

  <h2>Service</h2>
  <p>Termsinator provides automated summaries and risk scores for publicly available terms, privacy policies, and related documents. Results may be incomplete, outdated, or incorrect.</p>

  <h2>No legal advice</h2>
  <p>Termsinator does not provide legal advice and does not create a lawyer-client relationship. You are responsible for deciding whether to use a service and, where necessary, obtaining professional advice.</p>

  <h2>Submissions</h2>
  <p>You may submit URLs for public websites that Termsinator can lawfully access. Do not submit private network addresses, credentials, personal documents, or URLs intended to bypass access controls. Requests may be rejected, combined with an existing request, or rate-limited.</p>

  <h2>Reports</h2>
  <p>Reports describe what automated models found in a particular document revision. They do not establish that a company acted unlawfully or maliciously. Source citations, model identities, dates, coverage, and disagreements form part of each report.</p>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>The service is provided as available, without a guarantee of uptime, accuracy, or continued availability. Reports may be corrected, quarantined, or removed when evidence is invalid or a legitimate dispute is reviewed.</p>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>The software source is available under the license contained in the Termsinator repository. These service terms do not replace that software license.</p>
</Base>
